                <pb facs="1097" n="1001" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg1001"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0667/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-22T15:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1926—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Diplomatic body has requested me to join in signing collective note to the
                    Turkish Government requesting that diplomatic and consular officers be exempted
                    from the payment of consumption and other special taxes recently enacted. The
                    note is based essentially on international usage and courtesy. I recommend that
                    I be permitted to join body in making these recommendations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
